# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A filter variable operand reads a name, then parameters"

# filters.js ends a `<` or `(` operand at the first `>` or `)` and hands the text to
# parseFilterVariable (parseutils.js), which splits it at the first whitespace: a name, then the
# rest read as a call's parameters by parseMacroParameters. So `<now [UTC]YYYY0MM0DD>` calls `now`
# with a date format, and a literal bracket inside that format belongs to the parameter string —
# never to the filter run around it.

{{{ [[$:/temp/]addsuffix<now [UTC]YYYY0MM0DD0hh0mm0ssXXX]>] }}}
#                        ^^^ entity.name.variable.filter.operand.tiddlywiki5
#                        ^^^ - string.unquoted.html.tiddlywiki5
#                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ string.unquoted.html.tiddlywiki5
#                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ - entity.name.variable.filter.operand.tiddlywiki5

# The multi-valued operand splits the same way.
{{{ [tag(list sep)] }}}
#        ^^^^ entity.name.variable.filter.operand.tiddlywiki5
#             ^^^ string.unquoted.html.tiddlywiki5

# A named parameter reads as a call's named argument.
{{{ [<greet who:world>] }}}
#     ^^^^^ entity.name.variable.filter.operand.tiddlywiki5
#           ^^^ entity.other.attribute-name.argument.tiddlywiki5
#               ^^^^^ string.unquoted.html.tiddlywiki5

# CONTROL: a variable with no whitespace stays one name.
{{{ [tag<currentTiddler>] }}}
#        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ entity.name.variable.filter.operand.tiddlywiki5
#        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ - string.unquoted.html.tiddlywiki5

{{{ [tag(multiValued)] }}}
#        ^^^^^^^^^^^ entity.name.variable.filter.operand.tiddlywiki5
